}, {"text": "- **Unanchored Condition Terms Default to DiseaseClass:** IF a condition-denoting phrase (a bare head noun, a descriptive or pathological noun phrase, or an \"X of Y\" state noun phrase) occurs in a non-prenominal position, such as a complement or adjunct that describes a manifestation, consequence, association, or characterization, AND it contains no proper-name or eponymic anchor, no site-plus-disease compound, and no disease/syndrome/dysplasia head identifying a particular disorder, THEN label the span **DiseaseClass**, regardless of whether the surrounding clause is descriptive rather than nominal.\n  - **Negative Constraint:** Do NOT apply this rule when:\n    - (a) The phrase is anchored to a named disease (eponym, proper name, or named-entity head). Label it **SpecificDisease**.\n    - (b) The phrase is prenominal and modifies a following noun, such as a noun-noun compound or attributive premodifier. Label it **Modifier**.\n    - (c) The span is part of a coordinated or multi-condition construction that refers to several conditions at once. Label it **CompositeMention**.\n    - (d) The phrase denotes a non-condition entity, such as an anatomical structure, gene, drug, or measurement, rather than a condition.\n  - **Validity Check:** The rule keeps Modifier, SpecificDisease, and CompositeMention distinct by using prenominal position, anchoring, and coordination as the deciding tests. It does not alter any entity definition.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2432, "output_tokens": 2408, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1893}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}